# Preview slide move lock (do not regress)

Anthony (2026-11-02): extra knowledge checks in module 4 needed to sit with the other check at the end of the module, without a TOC drag rewrite.

`npm test` must stay green (`src/lib/courseSlideEdits.test.ts`).

## Invariants (code, not comments)

- **Edit → Move up / Move down.** [`handleMoveCurrentSlide`](src/App.tsx) is in the preview Edit menu. The menu stays open so authors can tap several times. Do not add TOC click-and-drag or an unlocked-contents mode.
- **Same module only.** [`moveSlideInCourse`](src/lib/courseSlideEdits.ts) swaps with the neighbor in `modules[i].slides`. It does not cross modules or move injected chrome (cover, overview, hub, exam).
- **Stay on the slide.** After a move, [`pendingSlideFocusId`](src/App.tsx) keeps the author on that slide’s new player index. Undo still restores the previous order.
- **Same gate as Delete.** Only [`isDeletableCourseSlide`](src/lib/courseSlideEdits.ts) rows move. System slides stay put.

## How to change this

Change `moveSlideInCourse` / the Edit menu items and add a failing test first. Do not “fix” order by regenerating the module.
